{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfj7nvvwBVaQQcfFb2HRM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I rewrote all three files for this repair slot with a new mechanism, and the self-check prints `OK`. It's a 100-draw, single-chain smoke fit with finite ELPD-LOO of −2098.6. I didn't run admission's full fit, so convergence and novelty are still unchecked, and this slot gets no further attempt.\n\n**Why I dropped the previous model.** It didn't converge: 9000 of 12000 transitions were divergent and R-hat reached 9.3. The likely cause is its decay weighting `exp(-rho·lag)`, which blows up when `rho` is negative. I didn't just fix that, because the mechanism itself (later flips counting more or less than earlier ones) is already in the set as `attention_gradient_sequential_evidence`. A fixed version would probably have been rejected as a near-duplicate.\n\n**New model: `occam_neglect_trick_coin_fit`.** This follows the brief: a normative account plus exactly one distortion.\n- **Base:** the same structure as the current best model, `second_order_chance_motif_suspicion`, which is known to converge.\n- **The distortion:** a properly Bayesian judge averages over every rate a trick coin might have, which automatically penalises flexible explanations. Here people partly neglect that penalty. They give the switch-biased and heads-biased coins a fitted share `omega` (between 0 and 1) of the rate that best fits the sequence in front of them.\n- **Effect:** a tailor-made trick coin can \"explain\" any mildly lopsided or streaky sequence, so those sequences look less random than the normative account predicts. At `omega = 0` the model reduces to the normative one.\n- **Cost:** one extra parameter with a smooth logit-normal prior. The two new per-sequence features are computed once in `prepare_observed`, so the sampling geometry should stay close to the base model's.\n\n**Caveats.**\n- The smoke ELPD of −2098.6 looks better than the best model's −2105.0, but the two numbers aren't comparable. One is a short smoke fit and the other a production fit.\n- The novelty gate requires predictions at least 0.002 RMSE from every live model. If `omega` is fitted near 0, the model predicts almost exactly like its base and would be rejected as a near-duplicate.\n\nFiles are in `/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/iter_3/candidate_2_repair_1/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2351,"cache_read_input_tokens":81977,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2351,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2c275ea1-d170-4189-8cfa-c3d763671f7c","uuid":"73241fc9-6ec6-4de1-9fc0-a486b457fdd9","timestamp":"2026-10-05T12:49:36.192Z","request_id":"req_011Cfj7nvSB2Y7hztBQDSVcC"}
